Let's use the information we have to represent the distance Wilmer walked when he went up the hill and when he went down the hill. Since it is the same path, the two expressions are equal.

For example, Wilmer went up the hill for $x$ minutes at a speed of $y$ kilometers per minute, so the total distance uphill is $x\cdot y$ kilometers:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\left(x\,\text{minutes}\right)\left(y\,\dfrac{\text{kilometers}}{\text{minute}}\right)
\\\\
&=x\cdot y\,\cancel{\text{minutes}}\cdot\,\dfrac{\text{kilometers}}{\cancel{\text{minute}}}
\\\\
&=x\cdot y\,\text{kilometers}
\end{align}$
